# Who reviews what (CIS Software Supply Chain Benchmark v1.0 §1.1.6).
#
# `codeowners_coverage` read `unknown` for this repository, which the platform
# renders as "without one, a code-owner review requirement routes to nobody".
# Reporting that about four other repositories while having no file of its own
# is the posture this platform exists to make visible, so it starts here.
#
# **This is a single-operator estate, and this file says so plainly rather
# than inventing teams.** Every line resolves to the same person, which makes
# the coverage number 100% and makes it mean exactly one thing: nothing here
# is owned by nobody. It does not mean review is distributed, and a file that
# implied otherwise would be worse than no file.
#
# `codeowner_review_required` is deliberately still off. Turning it on with
# these lines would deadlock every pull request — GitHub refuses to count a
# self-approval, which is the same trap D-110 hit and recorded. This file is
# the routing; enabling the requirement is a decision for the day there is a
# second reviewer.
#
# Last match wins, so the catch-all goes first and the specific paths follow.

*                               @ToddGBenson

# --- The paths where a review actually changes the outcome -----------------
#
# Listed separately not because the owner differs but because a reviewer
# arriving at one of these should know it is one of these. They are the places
# where a mistake reaches production, another repository, or a credential.

# Anything that runs against the estate's own infrastructure. A wrong value in
# a pipeline definition applies to a live Concourse target, and the pipelines
# are where B-065 found credentials that `fly get-pipeline` hands back.
/deploy/                        @ToddGBenson

# What gets installed into other people's repositories. A template defect ships
# to every onboarded repository on the next save, and a workflow that ignores
# an exit code reports a clean scan for a scan that broke.
/workflow-templates/            @ToddGBenson
/actions/                       @ToddGBenson

# The composite action's own supply chain and the delivery path to GHCR.
/.github/workflows/             @ToddGBenson

# What a finding is allowed to mean. The adapters decide severity, and the
